{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: Site read-token reuse (R4 item 1) at exact head 96bb50e6dc2a5af68224542841eaee232e0fac43, tree e6540cbdb4a03ae978e6ce022e41fb78edc92514, on builder/security-r4-site-token-reuse-20261025 (review request ef483901, my promise 1ba5d9b1). This report binds child request a084acc9 (promise 2e1ab66c) only; broader request 90878601 and the member quota stay open. One finding blocks: the head has no passing ordinary gate at its production and test bytes. Everything else is verified below, so the next review needs only the gate record and any byte change.\n\nBlocking finding: the one ordinary gate (58930) ran at commit 57ed0780 (tree 438e5c65) and failed seven Site cases in five files (application-publication, demo, edit, file-publication and site-native3). The repair then changed test fixtures (ebaae23932) and production twice: worker.ts at 73b1ae2a5d, and token-reuse.ts with worker.ts at a38dec604e. After those production changes only the three Scope compile contexts, the five custody cases in site-token-reuse.test.ts, and the entry-points, settings and Counting Node steps ran. The seven repaired Site cases, the other 490 files of the suite, and 37 of the 40 compile contexts have not run on the head's production bytes (tree 7c25d13e at 81261e42df, identical to the head in production, tests and seal map). Three of the unrun contexts compile packages/scope sources from outside the package: apps/room/page/tsconfig.scope.json, packages/cli/tsconfig.scope.json and packages/mcp/tsconfig.scope.json. docs/testing.md says to run the gate once at the head you will send; its two exceptions cover a commit that changes only documents and a gate failure repaired by only a document, and neither covers a repair that changes worker.ts. It also says a focused pass does not replace the final gate. The builder's note is honest about this (\"It does not turn any earlier failed invocation into a whole-gate pass\") and the request asks for no gate-0 claim, but approval needs one. Requested: run the ordinary gate once at this exact head, or at a later head whose production, test and seal-map bytes equal 81261e42df's; record result.json, stdout and the before/after records with digests in the evidence index; refile the review request. This is not a repeated suite: the only gate so far ran on other production bytes and failed.\n\nMy own targeted run at the head, for the builder's and planner's information and not as a substitute: the seven files the gate failed or the head added (the five fixture files, site-route.test.ts and site-token-reuse.test.ts) with the repository's Vitest and the pool compatibility step, observed run of 62.38 s wall: 7 files passed, 31 tests passed, 1 skipped, 0 failed; the worktree was clean afterwards. Log at the checker's scratchpad r4-96bb-myrun-vitest.log, SHA256 prefix 5beb5e0efc57b07b.\n\nRead order: the primary note first and in full (notes/implementation/2026-10-25-site-token-reuse.md; the request text named the demo test artifact as primary, the request body and the builder's correction fbe59a99 name the note), then the review request, the child request, the builder's promise, the planner ruling 3fdb03b9 and the broader request; then token-reuse.ts in full, the host.ts, route.ts and worker.ts diffs, the five custody tests in full, the site-route, worker harness, application-publication and four apps/room fixture diffs, the two docs and the seal map; then the evidence index and the audits it names.\n\nHead checks: the worktree is clean at the head on its branch; the merge-base with Main 6c0a9a4d is Main itself, so the 16 commits fast-forward and git merge-tree returns the head's own tree; 17 files, +642/-57; git diff --check is clean; check-commit-messages reports 16 checked, 0 flagged; the 17 artifact events at this head name exactly the 17 changed paths; the index's primarySource digest (62c868ca…) equals the note blob at the head.\n\nQualified evidence, verified: all 48 files named