e passes the branch ref for versions, the receipt ref for immutable reads and the selected ref otherwise, as the note says.\n- Caps. One transaction counts live rows and reserved mints before inserting a reservation: 256 keys and 32 mints refuse with capacity; followers refuse above 8 per flight and 64 in total; maintain deletes at most 256 expired rows per pass and never a live key. Capacity reaches the route as the existing unavailable refusal (503).\n- Hold. A reservation ends at start plus READ_TTL (120 s) plus 60 s, as ruling 3fdb03b9 permits; the finally block deletes it only when createToken was not entered, so an invalid or ambiguous answer after entry holds the key until that end; the flight deadline is the reservation end; a late answer cannot install because the UPDATE is a compare-and-set on key, generation, reserved state and unexpired end. No inline remint follows a 401 or network failure.\n- Expiry. The end comes from the provider's expiresAt, checked as a safe future time; #ready re-reads the row and requires end after now; nothing extends an end; wake() returns the earliest end and the alarm moves only earlier; alarm() runs maintain and reschedules. ScopeIndex had no other alarm user (worker.ts, scope-index.ts, serving-admission.ts), so the override displaces nothing.\n- Alarm failure after install. The row becomes unavailable with plaintext NULL and its known end kept; a later acquire reschedules and answers mint-pending; no mint until the row expires.\n- Local close. Opened.close drops the transport and empties secrets; no revoke; the source methods throw after close. Owner failures surface as SiteTokenUnavailable with no provider detail; provider step failures keep the StepError step and the unreadable refusal.\n- Readiness projection. The ScopeIndex callback reads ARTIFACTS_CONFIG, ARTIFACTS_NAMESPACE and ARTIFACTS afresh on each call, omits undefined optional strings, and decodes through artifactsReadiness; nothing is cached.\n- Tests. The five